        "The weather is milder than on the coast but not trivial. April and May are hot and dry at Puliyankudi's elevation of about 233 m, the south-west monsoon months bring steady, gusty winds through the nearby gap in the Ghats, and the north-east monsoon from October to December delivers most of the year's rain. Cambridge's October-November papers and the IB November session sit inside that wet window, so a power-cut plan is wise.",
        "Festivals are varied: Pongal in January, the Aadi season in July and August with the Aadi Thapasu festival at nearby Sankarankovil, Deepavali, Christmas, and the Muslim festivals of Ramadan and Eid. Ramadan and the Eids move roughly eleven days earlier each year, so a tutoring plan made once needs revisiting the next. Tutors can shift lesson times to suit fasting and prayer routines, which is easier to agree early than to improvise in the final fortnight before an exam.",
        "Lemon season shapes the family calendar more than the school one. Market mornings are busy, labour and transport are stretched, and a Class 11 student may be asked to help with the family trade at peak weeks. Agree in advance which weekly slot is safe, keep a lighter plan for harvest peaks than for quiet months, and pencil in a catch-up lesson before mocks.",
