  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there any IB or IGCSE school in Puliyankudi?", answer: "Not one that we could confirm. Schools in the municipality follow the Tamil Nadu State Board, Matriculation or CBSE, and the closest confirmed IB and Cambridge schools are in Madurai. Puliyankudi children who follow either syllabus normally do so through an online school, a hostel elsewhere or tutoring alongside a plan to switch. IB Gram supports each of those routes without needing a local school." },
    { question: "How do we find the right IB tutor for our child in Puliyankudi?", answer: "Start by telling us three things: the programme or board, the subject and level, and the next exam sitting. We come back with a tutor who has taught that course and book a free trial lesson at a time that works for your household. You see the teaching before agreeing to anything, and if the first fit is wrong we suggest another." },
    { question: "Which IGCSE boards do your tutors cover for students in Puliyankudi?", answer: "Both Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel. Cambridge candidates are matched by syllabus code and Core or Extended tier, and Edexcel candidates by specification and Foundation or Higher tier. Every lesson is online and built from that board's own past papers and mark schemes, so a student preparing Cambridge Chemistry 0620 is not taught from another board's worksheet." },
    { question: "Will a tutor come to our house in Puliyankudi?", answer: "No tutor travels to Puliyankudi; home visits are available only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. What we offer here is online home tuition: your child sits at home with a laptop while a private teacher appears on screen, with a shared whiteboard for every worked solution. The teaching is one to one, and only the delivery is digital." },
    { question: "How is the fee for IB or IGCSE tuition decided?", answer: "Programme and level, subject, lesson length, lessons per week and the tutor's recent experience with the exact syllabus set the fee, which you receive in writing before the free trial. Higher Level and Extended-tier work usually costs more than Core or primary support. We publish no price list, and no travel charge is added for Puliyankudi." },
    { question: "Our child studies at an online international school from Puliyankudi. What does a tutor add?", answer: "A live person who knows the syllabus. Online schools provide recorded lessons and platforms; a tutor checks understanding, marks practice papers, explains what a rubric wants and keeps the weekly pace. The school continues to teach and assess, while the tutor works alongside it, subject by subject, and reports progress to you in short written notes." },
    { question: "Our child boards in Madurai. Can lessons continue at home during holidays?", answer: "Yes. We match a tutor who has taught the subject and level your child's school uses, so a block in the Pongal or summer holidays continues the term's work. Some families book an intensive block before the school's mock examinations and a lighter weekly slot once term resumes." },
    { question: "What happens in the free trial lesson?", answer: "The proposed tutor teaches a real topic from your child's syllabus for a full lesson, online, and asks questions to see where understanding is secure and where it is not. You then receive a short written plan and a quoted rate. Nothing is paid for the trial, and you may decline, change tutor or continue." },
    { question: "Do your tutors help with Internal Assessments and the Extended Essay?", answer: "They coach; they do not write. A tutor can help your child narrow a topic, understand the criteria, structure a method and respond to a draft with honest feedback. Writing or rewriting any part of the assessed piece lies outside what an IB Gram tutor does, and the finished work must be your child's own." },
    { question: "Does online tutoring work when power or data is unreliable in Puliyankudi?", answer: "Mostly yes, with preparation. A charged laptop, a power bank and a second mobile data connection cover the usual interruptions, and a tutor can switch to audio and a photo of written working if video drops. We suggest agreeing beforehand how a lost lesson is made up, especially in the north-east monsoon weeks before exams." },
    { question: "My child studies in a Matriculation school. Is the jump to IB or IGCSE smaller?", answer: "Language is often easier, since Matriculation schools usually teach in English, but the habit change is the same: criteria-based marking, command words and coursework. A tutor spends the first weeks teaching the student to read a mark scheme as carefully as a textbook and to show reasoning in every answer." },
    { question: "Can lessons be planned around Ramadan, Pongal and festival weeks?", answer: "Yes. Slots are agreed with your household's calendar in mind: Ramadan hours, Eid, Pongal, the Aadi festivals, Deepavali and Christmas. For exam blocks we set the dates early so a festival week does not take out the final fortnight, and changes can be made at short notice with the tutor." },
    { question: "Do you teach IB MYP and PYP, or only the Diploma?", answer: "All stages. For PYP the focus is reading, number sense and Exhibition research in shorter, more frequent lessons. For MYP it is writing to criteria in Sciences and Language and Literature, mathematical reasoning and the Personal Project. Diploma and CP tutoring covers Maths, the sciences, Economics, English A and more." },
    { question: "When should we start, Grade 9 or Class 11?", answer: "As early as the syllabus begins: Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma. Early lessons repair foundations and teach the new habits before coursework deadlines and predicted grades arrive. Starting later still helps if lessons go to the highest-value topics and timed papers, and a short diagnostic lesson shows which approach suits your child." },
    { question: "What if my child and the tutor are not a good fit?", answer: "Tell us and we will introduce another tutor. A fit that is not working is a matching problem, not a reason to persevere. Families hear from us every few weeks to check progress, and a change can be made at any point, not only after the trial lesson." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any school, or to the IB, Cambridge or Pearson?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service. It has no partnership, sponsorship or endorsement arrangement with the schools named on this page, in Madurai, Thiruvananthapuram, Kodaikanal or anywhere else, nor with the IB, Cambridge University Press and Assessment or Pearson. Schools are listed only to show where options exist." },
  ],

